diff --git a/docs/development.md b/docs/development.md
index 0bca076..abbf133 100644
--- a/docs/development.md
+++ b/docs/development.md
@@ -72,6 +72,12 @@ bin/rails dev:email
 
 Under the hood, this will create or remove `tmp/email-dev.txt`.
 
+### Languages
+
+Fizzy speaks English (the default) and Japanese. Open any page with `?locale=ja` to switch: the choice is kept in the session and, once signed in, saved on the identity so it follows the person to their next device. A locale that isn't offered is ignored.
+
+Everything readable lives in `config/locales/`: `en.yml`/`ja.yml` for the app, mailers, models and JavaScript-facing strings, and `seeds.*.yml` for the onboarding Playground board. Views use lazy lookups (`t(".key")`), so keys mirror the view paths. When adding text, add it to both files — `I18n.available_locales` is the full list, and the static error pages in `public/` carry both languages inline since they're served without knowing who is looking.
+
 ## SaaS gem
 
 37signals bundles Fizzy with [`fizzy-saas`](https://github.com/basecamp/fizzy/tree/main/saas), a companion gem that links Fizzy with our billing system and contains our production setup.
